    <h2>But What If AI Makes a Mistake?</h2>

    <p>This is the number one objection. Fair enough — trust is earned.</p>

    <p>Here's how we handle it: AI pre-fills and drafts, humans review before anything goes live. You control the safety level. Want AI to send routine confirmations automatically? Fine. Want human approval for anything over $500? Also fine.</p>

    <p>The system is designed around human-in-the-loop principles. AI does the tedious work — data extraction, first drafts, status updates — but you maintain final approval on anything that matters. It's not about replacing judgment. It's about eliminating the drudgery that buries your judgment under busywork.</p>

